# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-lzh.md#block-header
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0064, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0068, PV-0073, PV-0350, PV-0351, PV-0352, PV-0354
# kind: decompress
# description: A block of type 0 (stored), which is not part of the LZH format.
# derivation: Header: length 1. Bits: 0-1 count 0; 2 final 1; 3-4 type 0 = 0,0; 5-7 zero, so byte 0 = 0x04. Byte 1 (0x41) is arbitrary and never reached. Type 0 fails with bad-block-type (PV-0073).
# expect.error: bad-block-type
# expect.algorithm: lzh
# expect.uncompressed_length: 1
hex:
01 00 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
12                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
02                                                # byte 7
04                                                # count 0, final 1, type 0
41                                                # arbitrary
